Vendor credit (conversion tools, v0.11+):

The `*_to_markdown` tool family (pdf_to_markdown, docx_to_markdown,
xlsx_to_markdown, pptx_to_markdown, image_to_markdown, audio_to_markdown,
youtube_to_markdown, bing_search_to_markdown, webpage_to_markdown,
git_repo_to_markdown) is a JavaScript/ESM port of the TypeScript
implementation in:

  markdownify-mcp by Zach Caceres
  https://github.com/zcaceres/markdownify-mcp
  Licensed under the MIT License.

The port lives at:
  - src/markdownify/utils.mjs       (port of utils.ts)
  - src/markdownify/markitdown.mjs  (port of Markdownify.ts)
  - src/tools/convert.mjs           (port of tools.ts + server.ts dispatch)
  - scripts/install-markitdown.mjs  (opt-in venv setup, `npm run install-markitdown`,
                                     equivalent to the upstream preinstall.sh)

Tool naming was adapted from kebab-case to snake_case for consistency with
the rest of the router's tool surface, and the `get-markdown-file` tool was
intentionally NOT ported (redundant with the router's `get_file`).

The actual file/URL → markdown conversion is performed by Microsoft's
`markitdown` Python CLI (https://github.com/microsoft/markitdown, MIT-licensed),
which the router invokes as a subprocess. Audio transcription, image OCR, and
some other extras require the `[all]` install (handled by `npm run install-markitdown`).

